\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The fixed-base native routine repeatedly raises its current residue to j, so the
exponent after stage j is j!, not lcm(1,...,j). It tests a gcd after every stage
and stops immediately at either a proper factor or complete collapse to n. A
factor’s base order dividing j! is sufficient to enter the gcd, but isolating
one factor also requires the other factors not to collapse simultaneously.
Reaching the largest prime of p-1 is not a general success condition. Original
smooth and safe-prime fixtures remain, with actual counterexamples to overbroad
claims.

$$ a_j=a_{j-1}^{\,j}\pmod n=2^{j!}\pmod n,\qquad d_j=\gcd(a_j-1,n). $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pollard_p_minus_1_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = dm::algorithms::pollard_p_minus_one_trace(391, 4);
    std::print("\n| actual j | residue before | actual powered residue | actual gcd |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.stages)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.j, r.before, r.after, r.gcd);

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first powering\nj={}, residue={}",
                       t.stages.front().j, t.stages.front().after));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual last powering\nj={}, residue={}",
                       t.stages.back().j, t.stages.back().after));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual proper gcd outcome\n{}", t.run.divisor));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pollard_p_minus_1_tiny.svg");
}
```
